# Fixed defect 131's class, 2026-09-29, beside the one-line suite: a `:` in
# mid-line where no body is written after it on its line. Symptom: `record
# P: i64` over its fields cost `trailing_colon` and then the head's junk, at
# the `i64`, and its certain fix wrote `record P i64`, still refused; a
# `function` head's `: i64`, TypeScript's result type, and an `if c: x`
# over a deeper block went the same way. Cause: the habit's reader took any
# `:` after a head. A `:` in mid-line is not the habit its fix repairs, and
# where it is not the suite over no block (`fixedbugs-131-a-colon-in-mid-line-
# over-no-block`), it is left to the head, whose own report of what goes on
# past its line names it once, the `:` first, and whose members or body
# below are read; no fix is certain, and `check --apply` leaves the file as
# it is (`selfhost/parse/colon_habit.hero`).

record P: i64  #~ expected_end_of_line
    x: i64

variant T: a  #~ expected_end_of_line

function result_after_a_colon() -> i64  #~ expected_end_of_line
    return 1

function a_body_on_its_head() -> i64: return 1  #~ missing_body

function a_block_below(n: i64)
    if n > 0: print(1)  #~ expected_end_of_line
        print(2)

function main()
    print(result_after_a_colon())

# Corrected 2026-09-30 by lane recovery-b1 (defect 131's class, lane X3's
# report): a `function` head's `: i64` is no longer left to the head. It is
# the result type's habit, told at the `:` as such, `-> i64` in its words,
# with the certain fix that writes `->`
# (`fixedbugs-131-a-result-type-after-a-colon` holds the others), so
# `check --apply` now writes that fix here and this case pins what it
# writes; the other colons are left as the header says.

# Moved 2026-10-04 with defect 198's repair (lane b9-recovery): `variant T: a`
# over nothing is told its `:` as the head's junk, beside its missing cases,
# where the junk waited for a case to be written below.

# Moved 2026-10-04 with defect 315's repair (lane b11-parse): the `a` past
# the `:` is the variant's case, written on its head's line, which the junk's
# report sends below; `empty_variant` beside it was that report's debris, and
# is not said (`parse/members_below.no_members_below`).
